WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.488 --> 00:00:01.718
Dismal reviews?

00:00:01.718 --> 00:00:02.910
Bad word-of-mouth?

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:06.815
Or was this historical epic just a little
too epic in length?

00:00:06.815 --> 00:00:10.785
Here's why Babylon bombed, and bombed big,
at the box office.

00:00:11.487 --> 00:00:17.939
Babylon had a production budget of $110 million,
which probably has gone to the huge cast as

00:00:17.939 --> 00:00:21.220
well as the intricate and decadent set designs.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.730
Colorful and sweeping, the film features plenty
of dizzying scenes of parties, revelers, and

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:32.079
mind-numbing hedonism, which probably helps
to explain where some of that budget went.

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:38.290
Unfortunately, the movie didn't do great during
its opening week, making a paltry $3.6 million

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.710
in 3,343 domestic theaters.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.219
Although still freshly released in theaters,
projections for Babylon are beginning to look

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:47.640
quite abysmal.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.230
Although many outlets weren't exactly projecting
a massive haul for Babylon, some expected

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.890
the film to make at least its money back.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:59.390
In late November, Box Office Pro predicted
that the movie would have both positives and

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.270
negatives that may affect its financial prowess.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:07.159
On the positive side, Babylon is a prestige
comedy with a star-studded cast.

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:11.619
On the negative side, the early reviews weren't
exactly the greatest, and historical films

00:01:11.619 --> 00:01:14.530
tend to be hit or miss with many audiences.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:19.340
They projected Babylon would make four to
nine million dollars in its first week, with

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.770
a grand total of between 18 to 39 million
in domestic totals.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.799
Gaming Zion made a bold, although somewhat
tempered bet on Babylon as well, saying that

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:33.533
gambling experts predicted a five- to six-million-dollar
opening weekend.

00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:36.522
"If I had money, I would only spend it on
things that were fun."

00:01:37.025 --> 00:01:41.660
As we mentioned earlier, some of the reviews
for Babylon weren't exactly strong, which

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.649
may have impacted theatergoers' willingness
to brave the winter weather and catch the

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:47.380
flick on the big screen.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:53.530
On Rotten Tomatoes, Babylon currently has
a 55% critic rating at the time of this writing.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:58.509
In their review of the film, Salon claimed
that Babylon is exhausting, finding that the

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:03.630
movie tries to do entirely too much over its
runtime, though ends up saying very little

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.420
by the movie's culmination.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:11.090
Similarly, Splice Today wrote that the first
90 minutes of Babylon is a hit in the making,

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:15.090
but unfortunately, the movie continues on
for another 90 minutes.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.200
Leonard Maltin offered a slightly more nuanced
take on the movie, and said,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.170
"I think what we have here in Hollywood is
high art."

00:02:30.731 --> 00:02:35.430
Many critics have pointed out the exceptionally
long runtime of the movie, which is three

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:39.140
hours and nine minutes of absolute heartbreak
and debauchery.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:43.730
A daunting endurance experience for viewers,
and one that may have proven to be too much

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.730
for some.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:49.480
Speaking with Collider, director Damien Chazelle
explained that editing the movie proved to

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:54.670
be a difficult process, saying that many of
the scenes were cut, but eventually restored,

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:58.091
and this became somewhat of a back-and-forth
throughout post-production.

00:02:58.442 --> 00:03:01.935
"I've been working on this movie for almost
15 years."

00:03:01.935 --> 00:03:07.810
Chazelle added that, at one point, Babylon
ballooned to three hours and 40 minutes, and

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.430
that he and the editing crew had to chip it
back down.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:11.440
Chazelle continued,

00:03:23.633 --> 00:03:26.474
"It's the biggest thing I've ever tried to
do."

00:03:26.699 --> 00:03:31.890
Another aspect that may impact box office
performance for Babylon is the negative feedback

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:37.526
loop created by articles claiming that the
movie has bombed or is in the process of doing so.

00:03:37.526 --> 00:03:42.519
Nobody is exactly champing at the bit to go
see a movie shrouded in negative articles,

00:03:42.519 --> 00:03:46.966
and one doesn't have to spend too much time
reading the news to see what we're talking about.

00:03:46.966 --> 00:03:50.830
Deadline ran an article with a headline that
claims that audiences were not jazzed for

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:56.230
Babylon, and that the movie has failed to
meet expectations, resulting in an unquestionably

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.900
massive box office bomb.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:03.370
Variety and Vanity Fair also mention Babylon
and its failure to generate significant revenue

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:05.060
during its opening run.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:10.090
Even Movie Web ran an article claiming that
Babylon is the second flop this year for star

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:14.860
Margot Robbie, noting that her ensemble movie
Amsterdam was also a misfire.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:19.380
These are just a few examples, but it does
highlight how negative press can have somewhat

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.380
of a snowball effect.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:23.820
"If you could go anywhere in the whole world,
where would you go?

00:04:24.337 --> 00:04:28.750
Perhaps the biggest reason why Babylon hasn't
attracted many large audiences comes down

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.009
to one big blue reason.

00:04:31.009 --> 00:04:36.070
Despite the fact that the holiday movie-going
experience doesn't exactly have too many adult-orientated

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:40.639
movies currently available, the success of
Babylon may have been hindered by the sequel

00:04:40.639 --> 00:04:44.690
to one of the biggest movies of all time — Avatar:
The Way of Water.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:49.580
A long-simmering continuation of the story
presented in Avatar, The Way of Water is slowly

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.750
charting its way to box office success.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.940
"We cannot let you bring your war here."

00:04:54.940 --> 00:05:01.289
As noted by The Numbers, Avatar: The Way of
Water is just shy of $1 billion in box office

00:05:01.289 --> 00:05:06.730
sales at the time of writing, which represents
the vast majority of theater-going experiences

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.360
over the past few weeks.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:12.660
The draw and spectacle of Avatar: The Way
of Water may have been enough to cut into

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:17.009
the audience that was initially interested
in Babylon, which may only represent a small

00:05:17.009 --> 00:05:18.600
sliver of ticket sales.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:23.070
However, families aren't exactly taking their
children to see a movie about the rise and

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:28.970
fall of 1920s Hollywood that ends on a relatively
dour note, at least when one considers that

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.760
specific period of time.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:35.169
Still, there seems to be a multitude of reasons
as to why Babylon has been unable to climb

00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:39.280
to the heights it had ambitions for, though
there certainly is a chance that the movie

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:42.700
will experience a resurgence in interest during
award season.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:47.889
Even though Babylon has been somewhat divisive
among critics, all agree on one thing: Margot

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:50.730
Robbie's performance is definitely worth some
accolades.

